From 88b1e8b34826bd24a7d8b5763306abcb1399f6d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 11:07:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PS4: the native memcpy's copies to and from GPU-cached memory
 happen; Memory::CopyBlock fixed

- Memory::CopyBlock walked the destination and wrote each piece of it onto itself: nothing was copied
  (inherited; its only callers were the kernel's I/O memory reads and writes). 04.75's native
  memcpy/memmove copied every piece touching a page that isn't plain memory (one the GPU caches) with
  it, so those copies did nothing: stale vertex/index/constant data (Echoes of Wisdom's flicker, its
  crash on a garbage index buffer, VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DEVICE_MEMORY). Now the native copy takes such a
  piece through a page buffer with ReadBlock and WriteBlock (the GPU's notifications), and CopyBlock
  walks the source and writes at the same offset in the destination.
- Move and Fill are templates over the memory type (tools/native-test checks them against memmove and
  memset with plain and GPU-cached pages: the 04.75 code 22% wrong, now none).
- EDEN_PS4_JIT_OFF=<names>: extras, pins, reuse, guard, leaf, native, each off alone (the menu's CPU >
  Speed-ups), logged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01W5pLthrq7391gS4qodPV4u
